/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 98 0 R
/E (Voting is one of the most important processes in a democratic system, as it allows citizens to choose their representatives fairly and freely. However, traditional voting methods such as paper ballots and ordinary Electronic Voting Machines \(EVMs\) suffer from several limitations including duplicate voting, fake identity usage, manual errors, longer processing time, and lack of transparency. These issues can reduce the reliability and efficiency of the election process.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
196 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 98 0 R
/E (To overcome these problems, this project presents an Advanced Electronic Voting Machine using Fingerprint Authentication and IoT technology. The main objective of this system is to provide a secure, transparent, and efficient voting process by ensuring that only authorized voters are allowed to cast their votes. In this system, a fingerprint sensor is used for voter verification, which prevents unauthorized access and eliminates the possibility of multiple voting by the same person.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
