216 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 99 0 R
/E (ESP32 is the central controller of the system with built-in Wi-Fi and multiple GPIOs. Initially, it is programmed via Arduino IDE and configured to communicate with all peripherals. It reads data from the fingerprint sensor and push buttons through serial and digital pins. It also drives the LCD using I2C communication. In the project, ESP32 performs authentication logic, vote counting, and data handling. It sends voting data to an IoT platform over Wi-Fi in real time. It ensures synchronization between input, processing, and output units. Overall, it acts as the brain of the voting machine)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
